// read_some with the count 0 is a runtime error that halts the program
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, Socket). The check comes before any wait: the peer sends
// nothing, so a call that waits first never ends and hits the timeout.
// STATUS: error
// TIMEOUT: 10
// CHECK: before
var srv = listen("127.0.0.1", 0);
var peer = connect("127.0.0.1", srv.port());
var conn = srv.accept();
print "before";
conn.read_some(0);
print "after";
